abstract:
In the paper, using Nevanlinna's value distribution theory of meromorphic functions in $\mathbb{C}^m$, we study for the existence of entire solutions $f$ in $\mathbb{C}^m$ of the following algebraic partial differential equation \[f^n(z)+P_d(f(z))=p(z)e^{\langle α,\ol zangle},\] where $P_d(f)$ is an algebraic differential polynomial in $f$ of degree $d \leq n-2$, $n \geq 3$ is an integer, $p$ is a non-zero polynomial, $α=(α_{1},\ldots,α_{m})
eq (0,\ldots,0)$ and $\langle α,\ol zangle=\sideset{}{_{k=1}^{m}}{\sum}α_{1k} z_k$. Also in the paper, we study for the non-existence of entire solutions $f$ in $\mathbb{C}^m$ of the following algebraic partial differential equation \[f^n(z)+P_d(f(z))=p_1(z)e^{\langle α, \ol zangle}+p_2(z)e^{\langle β, \ol zangle},\] where $P_d(f)$ is an algebraic differential polynomial of degree $d \leq n-3$, $n \geq 4$ is an integer, $p_1$ and $p_2$ are two non-zero polynomials, $α=(α_{11},\ldots,α_{1m})
eq (0,\ldots,0)$ and $β=(α_{21},\ldots,α_{2m})
eq (0,\ldots,0)$ such that $α_{1i}
eq 0$, $α_{2i}
eq 0$ and $α_{1i}/α_{2i}
ot\in\mathbb{Q}$ for all $i\in\mathbb{Z}[1,m]$. Our findings extend and improve the results of Li and Yang (J. Math. Anal. Appl., 320 (2006) 827-835) and Zhang and Liao (Taiwanese J. Math., 15 (5) (2011), 2145-2157) into higher dimensions.
